<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George VIII of Georgia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1417–1476</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as George I of Kakheti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George VIII was the last king of a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, reigning from 1446. Regional lords challenged him: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrat-vi-of-georgia">Bagrat of Imereti</a> defeated him at Chikhori in 1463, and in 1465 the atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samtskhe">Samtskhe</a> captured him. After his release he kept only Kakheti in the east, which he ruled as George I of Kakheti until 1476, and the kingdom split into Kartli, Kakheti, Imereti and Samtskhe.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-viii-of-georgia.jpg" alt="George VIII of Georgia" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George_VIII_of_Georgia_charter_1460.jpg: Digitized by the National Center of Manuscripts, Tbilisi, Georgia derivative... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_VIII_of_Georgia_charter_1460-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
